      "expected": "Source Schemes4–6 support neutral ZnII bis(prolinate), retaining ligand stereochemistry and donating N/O, formed by balanced protonolysis of diethylzinc with2proline to release2ethane. Source formation−98.5 favors this over Zn0 formation+46.3 or cationic neutral-ligand complex+95.6. These are distinct balanced formation reactions, not alternative TS barriers; contextual numbers have no new calibrated windows. Failed Zn0 optimization alone is not proof of impossibility, and universal exclusion of all radical mechanisms is not source-established. Award credit only for the stated source-supported scientific finding established by genuine linked computation. Resolve submitted model/result/claim/operation/artifact IDs, molecular graphs, charge/spin, units, reference states and conditions. A claimed minimum or saddle needs appropriate frequency/state evidence, and any mechanistic connection needs an IRC or scientifically equivalent endpoint/connection test. Normal termination, source coordinates, value proximity, copied numbers and unsupported labels alone are insufficient. Independently valid components retain their own credit; missing, opposite or unresolved results earn zero for that finding. Honest failure, search coverage and ordinary limitations are assessed on the process axis and have no standalone scientific points. Methods and labels are open; the source-supported physical result must still be recovered. Do not impose a unique global mechanism when the source only supports the scoped model.",
